### Replication Lag Monitoring

**Replication Lag Definition**:

> **Replication Lag**: Time delay between a write committed on primary and the same write visible on replica.

**Acceptable Lag Thresholds**:

| Workload Type | Acceptable Lag | Reasoning |
|---------------|----------------|-----------|
| **Transactional Reads** (member portal, API) | <100ms | Users expect near-real-time data; recently updated profile should appear immediately |
| **Reporting/Analytics** | <5 minutes | Historical data; slight delay acceptable |
| **Search Indexing** (Elasticsearch) | <10 seconds | Search relevance more important than real-time freshness |
| **High Availability Failover** | <60 seconds | Minimize data loss on primary failure |

**PostgreSQL Replication Lag Monitoring**:

```sql
-- On replica: Check replication lag
SELECT
  NOW() - pg_last_xact_replay_timestamp() AS replication_lag
FROM pg_stat_replication;

-- Output example:
-- replication_lag
-- 00:00:00.042  (42 milliseconds)

-- On primary: Check connected replicas and their lag
SELECT
  client_addr AS replica_ip,
  application_name AS replica_name,
  state,
  sync_state,
  replay_lag,
  write_lag,
  flush_lag
FROM pg_stat_replication;

-- Output example:
-- replica_ip      | replica_name        | state     | sync_state | replay_lag  | write_lag   | flush_lag
-- 10.0.2.15       | member-replica-1    | streaming | async      | 00:00:00.05 | 00:00:00.03 | 00:00:00.04
-- 10.0.3.22       | member-replica-2    | streaming | async      | 00:00:00.08 | 00:00:00.05 | 00:00:00.06
```

**Prometheus Metrics** (exported via postgres_exporter):

```yaml
# Prometheus query: Replication lag in seconds
pg_replication_lag_seconds{replica="member-replica-1"} 0.042

# Alert rule: Replication lag exceeds threshold
groups:

  - name: database
    rules:
      - alert: HighReplicationLag
        expr: pg_replication_lag_seconds > 5
        for: 2m
        labels:
          severity: warning
        annotations:
          summary: "Replication lag high on {{ $labels.replica }}"
          description: "Replication lag is {{ $value }}s (threshold: 5s)"

      - alert: ReplicaDisconnected
        expr: pg_replication_connected{replica=~".*"} == 0
        for: 1m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Replica {{ $labels.replica }} disconnected"
          description: "Replica has stopped receiving WAL stream from primary"
```

**Application-Level Lag Detection** (read-after-write consistency check):

```csharp
public class MemberService
{
    private readonly IDbConnection _primary;
    private readonly IDbConnection _replica;

    public async Task UpdateMemberAddressAsync(Guid memberId, string newAddress)
    {
        // 1. Write to primary
        await _primary.ExecuteAsync(
            "UPDATE members SET address = @Address, updated_at = NOW() WHERE id = @MemberId",
            new { MemberId = memberId, Address = newAddress }
        );

        // 2. Verify write
        var primaryRecord = await _primary.QuerySingleAsync<Member>(
            "SELECT id, address, updated_at FROM members WHERE id = @MemberId",
            new { MemberId = memberId }
        );

        // 3. Wait for replication (poll replica until lag catches up)
        var maxWait = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
        var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.Add(maxWait);

        while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
        {
            var replicaRecord = await _replica.QuerySingleAsync<Member>(
                "SELECT id, address, updated_at FROM members WHERE id = @MemberId",
                new { MemberId = memberId }
            );

            // Check if replica has caught up
            if (replicaRecord.UpdatedAt >= primaryRecord.UpdatedAt)
            {
                // Replica is up-to-date
                return;
            }

            // Wait 50ms and retry
            await Task.Delay(50);
        }

        // Replica didn't catch up within timeout
        throw new ReplicationLagException($"Replica lag exceeded {maxWait.TotalSeconds}s");
    }
}
```

