### Example 4: High Availability Failover (New York Incident)

**Scenario**: Primary database (East US) hardware failure; 7.2M New York members unable to access portal; need automatic failover to replica.

**Implementation**:

**Step 1: Configure Azure Auto-Failover**:

```bash
# Enable high availability with standby replica
az postgres flexible-server update \

  --resource-group gainwell-prod \
  --name member-service-primary \
  --high-availability Enabled \
  --standby-availability-zone 2

# Azure automatically:
# 1. Creates standby replica in different availability zone
# 2. Monitors primary health (TCP, SELECT 1 query every 10s)
# 3. Promotes standby if 3 consecutive health checks fail (30s detection)
# 4. Updates DNS to point to new primary
```

**Step 2: Simulate Failure** (testing in staging):

```bash
# Stop primary database (simulate hardware failure)
az postgres flexible-server stop \

  --resource-group gainwell-staging \
  --name member-service-primary

# Azure detects failure:
# - Health check 1 fails (10s)
# - Health check 2 fails (20s)
# - Health check 3 fails (30s) → Failover triggered

# Automatic promotion:
# - Standby replica promoted to primary (15-45s)
# - DNS updated: member-service-primary.postgres.database.azure.com → new IP
# - Old primary fenced (set read-only)

